+Role changes apply at the next refresh. An access token already issued stays valid until it
+expires (at most 15 minutes) unless the account's `security_version` changes: a password change
+or reset increments it, and `JwtAuthGuard` then refuses every older access token at once.
+`SessionsService.revokeAll(userId)`, and `endSessionsLocked(tx, userId)` inside a transaction that
+holds the user's lock, end every refresh session and raise it in the same transaction: use them
+for any other change that must end access at once (a role removed, an account disabled).
 
